<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Package xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        P1-D4b deploy manifest. Run it with the post-destructive flag and
        destructiveChangesPost.xml; see this directory's README.md.

        THIS MANIFEST IS NOT EMPTY, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE POINT (review W4, fixed
        2026-08-14). It lists exactly the eight files that `apply-d4.js b` edits.
        Until this fix it carried only a version element, while the README told the
        operator to run it with the post-destructive flag and argued that flag was
        correct BECAUSE the record type must be removed from the permission sets in
        the same run, before it is deleted. With no members those permission sets
        were not in the run at all: the org copies would still carry
        Opportunity.Commercial in their recordTypeVisibilities at the moment the
        destructive half fired, and the delete is refused.

        ORDER WITHIN ONE RUN, which is what the post-destructive flag buys:
          1. these eight files deploy, so Commercial disappears from both permission
             sets, from both Deal_Type__c value sets, and from the four record-type
             enumerations
          2. destructiveChangesPost.xml runs, deleting the Commercial RecordType and
             BusinessProcess, now referenced by nothing

        The pre-destructive flag is NOT equivalent: it would delete the record type
        while the org's permission sets still name it.

        NOTE the Commercial RecordType and BusinessProcess are deliberately ABSENT
        below. They belong to destructiveChangesPost.xml, and naming a member in both
        files is a contradiction.
    -->
    <types>
        <members>Lead.Deal_Type__c</members>
        <members>Opportunity.Deal_Type__c</members>
        <name>CustomField</name>
    </types>
    <types>
        <members>Lead.Acquisition_Broker</members>
        <members>Lead.IR_Investor</members>
        <members>Opportunity.Land</members>
        <members>Opportunity.Retail</members>
        <name>RecordType</name>
    </types>
    <types>
        <members>DPEG_Acquisition_Edit</members>
        <members>DPEG_Admin_Access</members>
        <name>PermissionSet</name>
    </types>
    <version>67.0</version>
</Package>
